cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
    If you use ASM Editor in teaching or research, please cite the
    EDUCON 2026 paper below.
title: ASM Editor
abstract: >-
    An educational IDE for assembly programming offering a unified
    multi-ISA workspace (M68K, MIPS, RISC-V, x86 and Z80), integrated
    debugging and visualization including backward execution, inline
    instruction documentation, and support for BYOD exams.
type: software
url: https://asm-editor.specy.app
repository-code: https://github.com/Specy/asm-editor
license: AGPL-3.0
